# EigenScript gap: one number type, so an integral float cannot be told from
# an integer (EigenScript#1286 row "One overloaded number type").
# Lua:      print(1, 1.0, 3 / 1, 2^53)  ->  1  1.0  3.0  9.007199254741e+15
#           math.type(1.0) -> float
# Expected: 1.0 stays distinguishable from 1 (a float/integer subtype).
# Actual v0.44.0:  1 / 1 / 3 / 9007199254740992 / 1 (str of 1.0 == str of 1)
# Rows: int_one_vs_one (D); also tbl/num printing of every float result.
print of 1
print of 1.0
print of (3 / 1)
print of (pow of [2, 53])
print of ((str of 1.0) == (str of 1))
